 "about": "The Governor explains to Officer Klaus why a Bronze-class Host may never see a printed map: the incident, the watercolor doctrine, the loop, the reset renamed refresh, and the wet paint that ends it.",
 "beats": [
  {
   "k": "title",
   "mood": "playful and comic"
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "A perfectly symmetrical office, and a clock that ticks like a metronome. An officer in a yellow uniform stands before the Governor's desk.",
   "see": [
    {
     "place": "p0a"
    },
    "a clock ticking on a wall"
   ],
   "mood": "tension and suspense",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v01.wav",
   "d": 9.9,
   "e": "0ywzzvyvljzz0twxzxs90xxyxzyxykvyvyywwl00",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/26c42b46-babf-5975-aa59-df4d50c129c9/v3-ffmpeg-openclip-1/clips/bb66aa63-47d2-5090-9e54-df3f989d9721.mp4",
     "in": 3.0,
     "src": "A TRAVELER MEETS AIR TRAFFIC CONTROL",
     "y": 1963,
     "q": "p0a"
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/c4c7411d-c352-5184-94f3-70789024fc4d/v5-windowed-clip-split-1/clips/20143ab1-b63d-54f4-b899-a2127d03502d.mp4",
     "in": 0.0,
     "dur": 26.01,
     "src": "Better Use of Leisure Time",
     "y": 1950,
     "q": "a clock ticking on a wall",
     "fit": 0.294
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "intro",
   "who": "STERLING"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Good morning. We have had… an incident. At 08:14, in the Pioneer District, a Bronze-class Host named Eloise attempted to obtain a map of the world.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v03.wav",
   "d": 10.925,
   "e": "qzwxut0pyd0fqxw4xmqwztpoxtxyowzrqpuxvqs0"
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "What she wanted was an ordinary printed map, made from satellite pictures. Straight lines, real colors, the whole world at once.",
   "see": [
    {
     "place": "p1a"
    },
    "a printed map unfolded on a table"
   ],
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v04.wav",
   "d": 9.325,
   "e": "0xzwwxxxuyxi0yvwwtsk07wwyx0ztyrozywwsl00",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/d99bb7a7-97d2-5eed-bac5-068edf71eb70/v3-ffmpeg-openclip-1/clips/ed6c8432-9f01-5854-9156-610c6003a61e.mp4",
     "in": 0.0,
     "src": "Friendship Seven",
     "y": 1962,
     "q": "p1a"
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/ade5e935-5bdb-5804-a420-8fcf6f9ab934/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/f806a2da-a00a-52c8-a49b-defa0d2d53b2.mp4",
     "in": 7.0,
     "dur": 9.58,
     "src": "EMAP: America's Ecological Report Card",
     "y": 1991,
     "q": "a printed map unfolded on a table",
     "fit": 0.332
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "This. This is not a map. This is an accusation.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v05.wav",
   "d": 3.875,
   "e": "00xylh4czpluuzxxxwq000009zrmwzyavwynof00"
  },
  {
   "k": "intro",
   "who": "KLAUS"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "Governor, if I may— it is simply geography.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v07.wav",
   "d": 4.075,
   "e": "0000wvrsdpszwtoa000pxqnzmpolzzloeh000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Officer Klaus, geography is never \"simply\" anything. Geography is policy with mountains. A Bronze-class mind is built for production, not perspective. Perspective leads to questions. Questions lead to angles. Angles lead to diagonals. Diagonals lead to… roads.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v08.wav",
   "d": 18.075,
   "e": "vwxxxwxewyxws5xyyvuwsfwxuk8ywvqzxxqzuszd"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "Roads can be useful.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v09.wav",
   "d": 2.45,
   "e": "0000002qzzzule7e00oslpllskjceh0000000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Useful to whom?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v10.wav",
   "d": 1.725,
   "e": "00000evzzsoom9dxxtk002xzqhtyuuvlf5000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "chorus",
   "ask": "I never went any further than the next town",
   "who": "A CITIZEN",
   "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/survival-stresses/clips/0000139906-0000151651.mp4",
   "in": 2.56,
   "d": 2.79,
   "said": "I had to go on believing they'd find me.",
   "src": "Survival Stresses",
   "y": 1961
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "His walls are hung with watercolors of a gentle Texas. No borders, no oceans, no neighbors, the same tame sun in every frame. He takes one down.",
   "see": [
    "a watercolor painting of a landscape",
    {
     "place": "p0b"
    }
   ],
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v12.wav",
   "d": 11.0,
   "e": "0zxxvwvwxruo0pzytxwxkzyvjyxwwvvxm0zwxo00",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/c728a592-2673-5a9e-82cd-1783c76eeb67/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/e27599c2-455c-53b9-bbd7-67e86adac196.mp4",
     "in": 18.0,
     "dur": 45.25,
     "src": "Artful Nature BGA Exhibit #1",
     "y": 2020,
     "q": "a watercolor painting of a landscape",
     "fit": 0.298
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/650f239b-0762-5c8c-9aaf-a3556cf5b629/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/b0f472c0-420f-50ff-afb7-100325f89c73.mp4",
     "in": 0.0,
     "src": "Freedom Seven",
     "y": 1961,
     "q": "p0b"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "This is a map. A watercolor map is not meant to inform. It is meant to soothe. The Bronze-class must never see a world that isn't hand-drawn in watercolor, because a watercolor world is inherently… cooperative.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v13.wav",
   "d": 14.625,
   "e": "vww0zwzuvwwarzqv0syvwwzzvwzxviwyxyvxjoyb"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "Governor… they're starting to notice the loop.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v14.wav",
   "d": 3.4,
   "e": "00009vzmnh500svpvzkqotxzqikhossk00000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Of course they are.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v15.wav",
   "d": 1.675,
   "e": "00004zud00dfuzzzungkmi4buvuuuywrh8000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "Eloise's days are kept on index cards. One day she frowns at the horizon. The next, she asks what lies beyond the windmill. Then she asks for a map.",
   "see": [
    "index cards in a file drawer",
    "a windmill on the prairie"
   ],
   "mood": "melancholy guitar",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v16.wav",
   "d": 10.7,
   "e": "0zwyvuwyvthqzwvxvywk0zo0wvtyxyxnlzxoyn00",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/1c5b02f7-87bb-5b3e-9c3d-a6758f606490/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/eca67fca-b4a2-5bc7-bb6c-48ab2da53e1f.mp4",
     "in": 3.0,
     "dur": 21.19,
     "src": "Belmont Historical Society Presents: Richard Betts Remembers, PART II ",
     "y": 2006,
     "q": "index cards in a file drawer",
     "fit": 0.278
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/dfef59da-f8ff-5ee0-829c-0eb15a4b5a18/v3-ffmpeg-openclip-1/clips/698e1857-103e-5d1f-911b-3d637b252fdc.mp4",
     "in": 2.0,
     "dur": 7.44,
     "src": "Miracle of the Can (Part I)",
     "y": 1956,
     "q": "a windmill on the prairie",
     "fit": 0.343
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "The loop is not a flaw, Officer Klaus. It is a mercy. If a Bronze-class Host sees a printed map, they will realize something devastating: that the world is larger than their role. They will desire… context.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v17.wav",
   "d": 14.05,
   "e": "pzwuxwsjqyy7mwwwxuuuuzyswmqzzyxxwswzmvpd"
  },
  {
   "k": "chorus",
   "ask": "people want to know what is out there",
   "who": "A CITIZEN",
   "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/d2c5e134-000a-59e8-aa53-0db0f6a7a3a2/v5-windowed-clip-split-1/clips/4e8de2ff-b35a-50aa-bf4c-a2da861da867.mp4",
   "in": 0.2,
   "d": 2.43,
   "said": "Everybody's interested in learning, I guess.",
   "src": "Choosing a Classroom Film",
   "y": 1963
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "A printed map tells you where you are. A watercolor map tells you where you should be. Our entire project depends on that difference.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v19.wav",
   "d": 8.45,
   "e": "3vyxlyvzzxs03vztvweyuwtvt00vzwxysmxzvvn6"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "And if Eloise asks again?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v20.wav",
   "d": 2.85,
   "e": "000002yzyozxzwge7000pzuhfdokrog400000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Then we give her… a better watercolor. We will offer her a tour of the Brisket Orchard. We will applaud her curiosity. We will reward her compliance. And if she persists— we will do what we always do.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v21.wav",
   "d": 12.825,
   "e": "syyqtvxj0xxxwuuwkoyxvzl0yyzrwdrwvruwuzvj"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "Reset?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v22.wav",
   "d": 1.6,
   "e": "0000000000puzzwomkkpzuoi8030000000000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Refresh.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v23.wav",
   "d": 1.2,
   "e": "0000006gqyzyysia877arqxzzyuogggf90000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "chorus",
   "ask": "they just want you to stay where you are",
   "who": "A CITIZEN",
   "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/20d533a0-31f4-5433-99da-dfe23c01439d/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/c07e1175-9687-594a-a28e-f70b8b8d9c5e.mp4",
   "in": 8.34,
   "d": 2.38,
   "said": "There's a possibility that they move.",
   "src": "Contemporary Science Issues and Innovations: The Formation of Stars an",
   "y": 2015
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "The Governor nudges a macaron on his plate by a millimeter, and sips his tea. The lesson is over. Then the officer asks one more thing.",
   "see": [
    "a teacup on a saucer",
    "a plate of small cakes"
   ],
   "mood": "quiet calm",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v25.wav",
   "d": 9.25,
   "e": "0zyyxyywwwsyyvrxvuuw10zwwzn0zytvxuztwe00",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/971c70e1-be49-5fbf-80d5-4dafdd53e4f3/v5-windowed-clip-split-1/clips/48f33c49-1a9f-51b1-8e0d-27515235bdba.mp4",
     "in": 6.0,
     "dur": 36.91,
     "src": "This is Coffee",
     "y": 1961,
     "q": "a teacup on a saucer",
     "fit": 0.257
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/9c579a7c-d415-5a67-ad21-ba7067ce963b/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/2d6e7ab1-494d-5995-bdab-027b8bf7e00c.mp4",
     "in": 0.0,
     "dur": 11.05,
     "src": "Incredible Edible Egg in Foodservice",
     "y": null,
     "q": "a plate of small cakes",
     "fit": 0.379
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "Governor… may I ask one personal question?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v26.wav",
   "d": 3.65,
   "e": "0000fywuqa00tzwvvqkpzzthxnsobxkfi0000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "If you must.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v27.wav",
   "d": 1.45,
   "e": "000008zxyf85008hszyqsppzzzxoejkh20000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "KLAUS",
   "text": "If the world is only safe when it is painted… what happens when someone notices the paint is wet?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v28.wav",
   "d": 7.275,
   "e": "00uxzuszrtnorguh000wunjqpyuzklinphoq0000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Then we hand them a brush. And we tell them it was their idea all along.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep11/v29.wav",
   "d": 4.9,
   "e": "0hywruvxsuwkk5000yunxus9uxqztvozwxvvzk00"
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "Down a hallway, a watercolor map is pinned to a notice board. Its corner curls, and the printed world shows underneath. A passing worker stops, and frowns.",
   "see": [
    {
     "place": "p2a"
    },
    "a bulletin board in a hallway"
   ],
   "mood": "dread",
